    <briefdescription>
<para>A builder class that knows how to construct <ref refid="classllvm_1_1mca_1_1_instruction" kindref="compound">Instruction</ref> objects. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Every llvm-mca <ref refid="classllvm_1_1mca_1_1_instruction" kindref="compound">Instruction</ref> is described by an object of class <ref refid="structllvm_1_1mca_1_1_instr_desc" kindref="compound">InstrDesc</ref>. An <ref refid="structllvm_1_1mca_1_1_instr_desc" kindref="compound">InstrDesc</ref> describes which registers are read/written by the instruction, as well as the instruction latency and hardware resources consumed.</para>
<para>This class is used by the tool to construct Instructions and instruction descriptors (i.e. <ref refid="structllvm_1_1mca_1_1_instr_desc" kindref="compound">InstrDesc</ref> objects). Information from the machine scheduling model is used to identify processor resources that are consumed by an instruction. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
